w(f"\n**The precision was wrong.** The title share has been quoted as about 22 percent give or take 0.4. One constant in the simulator, how much a team's categories rise and fall together week to week, was set by judgment and never measured. Turning it off gives about {sv(SH0, RS['seeds'][0]):.0f} percent; doubling it gives about {sv(SH2, RS['seeds'][0]):.0f}. So read the title share as about {REF[str(RS['seeds'][0])]:.0f} give or take 3 on the simulator as it now stands. The league-format assumptions barely matter, and they are no longer assumptions: your settings page is on file and the simulator matches it.")
